{"term":"плотский","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"plotskiy","category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"carnal_desire","concept":"carnal_desire","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"literary","crude":10,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Russian adjective meaning 'carnal' or 'of the flesh'; refers to physical, especially sexual, desires and pleasures as contrasted with spiritual ones.","english_term":"carnal","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Плотские грехи' (carnal sins) and 'плотские желания' (carnal desires) are standard collocations; the binary 'плотское vs. духовное' (carnal vs. spiritual) is central to Russian Orthodox moral theology."}
